[{:db/id 17592186100923 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5a60deb5-551b-564a-a9a5-424f5c35cb79" "question-35ba1238-9d03-56c3-a9e7-b912f69594b6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100922 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-026fc717-7ff3-5e33-aea2-f16023ff29e1" "question-abf79c71-49dc-5540-8e88-cbf4204858e9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5a60deb5-551b-564a-a9a5-424f5c35cb79" :question/id #uuid "5a60deb5-551b-564a-a9a5-424f5c35cb79" :question/math-academy-id "q-17554" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the following equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{y(y-1)}{x}=0\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the substitution* $z={y}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{-1}\\,⟹\\,y={z}^{-1}\\,\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ with the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{{z}^{-1}({z}^{-1}-1)}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{z({z}^{-1}-1)}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1-z}{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. First, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1-z}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{z}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{dz}{dx}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\ x\\frac{dz}{dx}+z & =1 \\\\ \\frac{d}{dx}(zx) & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(zx)\\,dx & =\\int 1\\,dx \\\\ zx & =x+C \\\\ z & =\\frac{x+C}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =\\frac{x+C}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{x+C}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fc48d748-c473-5089-bb17-fc3ad8129f55"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fc48d748-c473-5089-bb17-fc3ad8129f55" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc48d748-c473-5089-bb17-fc3ad8129f55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cde43acc-0b98-5113-aa21-f90fd88d5eb9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-07e8f688-4e1e-5c56-97f0-ebcb8599d2bf" "answer-b4d45c86-e566-5b1e-8a2b-c81f4e145b01" "answer-67100b80-0a22-513b-a893-f811e8dbb561" "answer-ef914b0e-cc6b-5a2c-bbbd-fc5145c04181" "answer-cde43acc-0b98-5113-aa21-f90fd88d5eb9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07e8f688-4e1e-5c56-97f0-ebcb8599d2bf" :answer/id #uuid "07e8f688-4e1e-5c56-97f0-ebcb8599d2bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{x+C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4d45c86-e566-5b1e-8a2b-c81f4e145b01" :answer/id #uuid "b4d45c86-e566-5b1e-8a2b-c81f4e145b01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{-1+Cx}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67100b80-0a22-513b-a893-f811e8dbb561" :answer/id #uuid "67100b80-0a22-513b-a893-f811e8dbb561" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{1+Cx}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef914b0e-cc6b-5a2c-bbbd-fc5145c04181" :answer/id #uuid "ef914b0e-cc6b-5a2c-bbbd-fc5145c04181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{1+C{e}^{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cde43acc-0b98-5113-aa21-f90fd88d5eb9" :answer/id #uuid "cde43acc-0b98-5113-aa21-f90fd88d5eb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{x+C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-35ba1238-9d03-56c3-a9e7-b912f69594b6" :question/id #uuid "35ba1238-9d03-56c3-a9e7-b912f69594b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-168136" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the following equation. \n\n$$\nx\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}-y\\,,\\,x>0\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the substitution $z={y}^{3}.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,y={z}^{1/3}\\,.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $y(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3{z}^{2/3}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, the original differential equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{1}{3{z}^{2/3}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}) & =\\frac{1}{{z}^{2/3}}-{z}^{1/3} \\\\ \\frac{x}{3{z}^{2/3}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{z}^{2/3}}-{z}^{1/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. First, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{3{z}^{2/3}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{z}^{2/3}}-{z}^{1/3} \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1-z \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}\\,z & =\\frac{3}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{3}{x},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{3}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 3/xdx} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{3}} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUnder the condition that $x>0.$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{3}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}\\,z) & ={x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}z & =3{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{x}^{3}z] & =3{x}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{x}^{3}z]\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {x}^{3}z & ={x}^{3}+C \\\\ z & =1+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{3}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3} & =1+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{1+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5a6c67e1-0333-5cc2-869a-1bbcb67a5ad4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5a6c67e1-0333-5cc2-869a-1bbcb67a5ad4" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a6c67e1-0333-5cc2-869a-1bbcb67a5ad4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e3e22341-e31a-501a-8fe5-17c1a3059d06" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f676f359-3bb2-5251-b3a3-8de1cb0f8efe" "answer-e3e22341-e31a-501a-8fe5-17c1a3059d06" "answer-312c49cf-0c6c-5892-8c0c-c8af9a9efdc0" "answer-be8c913a-72b2-55f0-b55f-c27cd2fff516" "answer-dd1682b0-1f15-5588-a64b-354bdccd5fab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f676f359-3bb2-5251-b3a3-8de1cb0f8efe" :answer/id #uuid "f676f359-3bb2-5251-b3a3-8de1cb0f8efe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+C}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3e22341-e31a-501a-8fe5-17c1a3059d06" :answer/id #uuid "e3e22341-e31a-501a-8fe5-17c1a3059d06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{1+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-312c49cf-0c6c-5892-8c0c-c8af9a9efdc0" :answer/id #uuid "312c49cf-0c6c-5892-8c0c-c8af9a9efdc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C+\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be8c913a-72b2-55f0-b55f-c27cd2fff516" :answer/id #uuid "be8c913a-72b2-55f0-b55f-c27cd2fff516" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x+C}{{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd1682b0-1f15-5588-a64b-354bdccd5fab" :answer/id #uuid "dd1682b0-1f15-5588-a64b-354bdccd5fab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{1+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-026fc717-7ff3-5e33-aea2-f16023ff29e1" :question/id #uuid "026fc717-7ff3-5e33-aea2-f16023ff29e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-79851" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{4}{x}y=-6{x}^{2}{y}^{3/2},\\,y(1)=\\frac{1}{9},\\,y>0.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{2}{x}\\,z=3{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nusing the substitution $z={y}^{-1/2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The substitution $z={y}^{-1/2}$ transforms the given equation into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{2}{x}\\,z=3{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition\n\n$$\nz(1)={(\\frac{1}{9})}^{-1/2}=3\\,.\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nP(x)=-\\frac{2}{x},\\,Q(x)=3{x}^{2}\\,.\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2\\int 1/x\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{-2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{-2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{2}{x}\\,z) & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\,z & =3 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,z) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,z)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,z & =3x+C \\\\ z & =3{x}^{3}+C{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we determine the value of $C$ that satisfies the initial condition $z(1)=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z(1) & =3 \\\\ 3(1)^{3}+C(1)^{2} & =3 \\\\ 3+C & =3 \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have \n\n$$\nz=3{x}^{3}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by substituting the solution into $z={y}^{-1/2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1/2} & =z \\\\ {y}^{-1/2} & =3{x}^{3} \\\\ {y}^{1/2} & =\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}} \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{9{x}^{6}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8efc61ad-4fda-52b5-938e-e4876d1543c4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8efc61ad-4fda-52b5-938e-e4876d1543c4" :answer-field/id #uuid "8efc61ad-4fda-52b5-938e-e4876d1543c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1c929e44-8fd2-5bf3-a591-593f963cc37a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60cdcd5a-5e26-5ad6-b900-442757f6cdb5" "answer-211a917f-20cc-5b51-a9e7-7937b4ee619a" "answer-1c929e44-8fd2-5bf3-a591-593f963cc37a" "answer-bd2f785d-2c42-57fc-8cb3-ec5c8133839c" "answer-307b98d2-24ae-5636-9ef4-195d3181bb13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60cdcd5a-5e26-5ad6-b900-442757f6cdb5" :answer/id #uuid "60cdcd5a-5e26-5ad6-b900-442757f6cdb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{(2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-211a917f-20cc-5b51-a9e7-7937b4ee619a" :answer/id #uuid "211a917f-20cc-5b51-a9e7-7937b4ee619a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{({x}^{3}+2)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c929e44-8fd2-5bf3-a591-593f963cc37a" :answer/id #uuid "1c929e44-8fd2-5bf3-a591-593f963cc37a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9{x}^{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd2f785d-2c42-57fc-8cb3-ec5c8133839c" :answer/id #uuid "bd2f785d-2c42-57fc-8cb3-ec5c8133839c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{3}{4{x}^{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-307b98d2-24ae-5636-9ef4-195d3181bb13" :answer/id #uuid "307b98d2-24ae-5636-9ef4-195d3181bb13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{(5{x}^{3}+{x}^{2})^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-abf79c71-49dc-5540-8e88-cbf4204858e9" :question/id #uuid "abf79c71-49dc-5540-8e88-cbf4204858e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-168139" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=xy,\\,y(1)=\\frac{1}{3},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that the given differential equation can be transformed into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nusing the substitution $z={y}^{-1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The substitution $z={y}^{-1}$ transforms the given equation into the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nunder the condition that $x>0.$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz) & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ xz & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C \\\\ z & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now determine $C$ from the initial condition  $y(1)=\\frac{1}{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+C} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{1}{0+C} \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0c2ae4a2-7aee-5a15-87d2-14ca2c8d362a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0c2ae4a2-7aee-5a15-87d2-14ca2c8d362a" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c2ae4a2-7aee-5a15-87d2-14ca2c8d362a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c089f48e-5eec-5164-9b80-a61e10c8f30b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5ce1a23c-a543-5a3a-976c-513bed73760b" "answer-d310da97-f3cf-5dae-870e-04cfe0711dde" "answer-3d4e3eb2-e031-5967-901f-7f694c829795" "answer-c089f48e-5eec-5164-9b80-a61e10c8f30b" "answer-b9618fff-b0d5-5622-add2-f2d1be8efb58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ce1a23c-a543-5a3a-976c-513bed73760b" :answer/id #uuid "5ce1a23c-a543-5a3a-976c-513bed73760b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}{6x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d310da97-f3cf-5dae-870e-04cfe0711dde" :answer/id #uuid "d310da97-f3cf-5dae-870e-04cfe0711dde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+3}{9{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d4e3eb2-e031-5967-901f-7f694c829795" :answer/id #uuid "3d4e3eb2-e031-5967-901f-7f694c829795" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c089f48e-5eec-5164-9b80-a61e10c8f30b" :answer/id #uuid "c089f48e-5eec-5164-9b80-a61e10c8f30b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9618fff-b0d5-5622-add2-f2d1be8efb58" :answer/id #uuid "b9618fff-b0d5-5622-add2-f2d1be8efb58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101031 :activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
